      "latency_ms": 2644.1,
      "prompt_tokens": 11,
      "completion_tokens": 603,
      "output": "At its simplest, **water** is a clear, odorless, and tasteless liquid that is essential for all known forms of life. \n\nTo truly understand what water is, we can look at it through a few different lenses: its chemical makeup, its unique physical properties, and its role in the universe.\n\n---\n\n### 1. The Chemistry of Water (H₂O)\nScientifically, water is a chemical compound made of two types of atoms: **Hydrogen** and **Oxygen**. \n* Its chemical formula is **$H_2O$**. \n* This means every single molecule of water is made up of **two hydrogen atoms** bonded to **one oxygen atom**.\n\n### 2. States of Matter\nWater is one of the few substances on Earth that naturally exists in three distinct forms (states of matter) depending on the temperature:\n* **Liquid:** The water we drink, swim in, and rain from the sky.\n* **Solid (Ice):** Frozen water, found in glaciers, snow, and ice cubes.\n* **Gas (Vapor/Steam):** Water in the air as an invisible gas, or visible as steam when boiled.\n\n### 3. Unique and Magical Properties\nWater has several bizarre and unique scientific properties that make life possible:\n* **The Universal Solvent:** Water can dissolve more substances than any other liquid. Because of this, it acts as a carrier, transporting vital chemicals, minerals, and nutrients wherever it goes (in rivers, in plant stems, and in our bloodstreams).\n* **Ice Floats:** Almost all liquids shrink and become denser when they freeze. Water, however, *expands* and becomes less dense when it turns to ice. This is why ice cubes float. In nature, this means lakes freeze from the top down, allowing fish and marine life to survive the winter underneath the ice.\n* **High Heat Capacity:** Water can absorb a lot of heat before its temperature changes significantly. This helps regulate the climate of the entire planet and keeps living bodies from overheating.\n* **Cohesion and Adhesion:** Water molecules like to stick to each other (cohesion—which creates surface tension, allowing bugs to walk on water) and to other things (adhesion—which is how water climbs up the roots of giant trees).\n\n### 4. Water and Life\nLife as we know it cannot exist without water. \n* **Biology:** The human body is made up of roughly 60% water. It cushions our brains, regulates our body temperature, and flushes out waste.\n* **Ecosystems:** Oceans, rivers, and lakes cover about **71% of the Earth's surface**, providing habitats for millions of species.\n\n### Summary\nWater is the ultimate building block of our world. It carved the Grand Canyon, fills our oceans, powers our weather systems, and flows through the veins of every living creature."
